# Where the cascade retraction lands: per action, not per firing
# ([RARC.5.6.8]). The vector
# logical/RARC.5.6.8_a_cascade_lands_between_two_emits holds the
# runtimes to the clause on this program; this holds them to each other.
# `two_emits` has two actions, and only the second invalidates
# `make_artifact`'s `no (…)`:
#
#   emit Bystander      -- no cascade
#   emit Refusal        -- retracts the already-emitted Artifact
#
# so they predict different traces:
#
#   per action (the clause)   assert Bystander, emit, RETRACT, assert Refusal, emit
#   per firing                assert Bystander, emit, assert Refusal, emit, RETRACT
assert Build id=1
assert RefusalText id=1
pump
